<< /A 46 0 R /Alt (Network diagram illustrating trophic interactions in a marine ecosystem, with nodes representing organisms such as phytoplankton, zooplankton, fishes, seaweeds, and bacteria. Node size varies by group abundance. Arrows of different thicknesses and colors indicate flow strength, with red representing the strongest flows and blue the weakest, as detailed in the color legend.   ) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
